1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,503
<i>They're living lavishly.</i>

2
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:05,880
<i>They have a beautiful house.</i>

3
00:00:05,964 --> 00:00:08,967
<i>They're living a luxurious life.</i>

4
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:14,014
[SOBS] <i>And now, they have your father too!</i>

5
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:16,057
<i>And what do we have?</i>

6
00:00:16,141 --> 00:00:18,393
<i>Nothing!</i>

7
00:00:18,476 --> 00:00:19,436
<i>Ma…</i>

8
00:00:20,645 --> 00:00:22,856
<i>Someone definitely tried</i>
<i>to leak the files.</i>

9
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:25,817
<i>Tough luck for them,</i>

10
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:28,361
<i>all of our confidential data is encrypted.</i>

11
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:30,363
<i>Anyone tries to hack, leak our files,</i>

12
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:31,614
<i>this will pop up.</i>

13
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:33,992
<i>There's not much we can do here.</i>

14
00:00:34,576 --> 00:00:35,744
<i>But I did my part,</i>

15
00:00:35,827 --> 00:00:38,246
<i>so please delete the photos.</i>

16
00:00:38,329 --> 00:00:39,539
<i>Not yet.</i>

17
00:00:40,165 --> 00:00:42,208
<i>What?! Are you kidding me?</i>

18
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:44,085
<i>This is not what we talked about!</i>

19
00:00:44,169 --> 00:00:46,421
<i>You said steal the files</i>
<i>and you'll delete the photos!</i>

20
00:00:46,504 --> 00:00:47,922
<i>And that's what I did!</i>

21
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:51,926
<i>You really think you scare me, Peter?</i>

22
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:53,219
<i>Hmm?</i>

23
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:54,929
<i>If I were you…</i>

24
00:00:57,223 --> 00:00:58,433
<i>I would behave.</i>

25
00:00:58,516 --> 00:00:59,893
<i>Or else,</i>

26
00:01:00,435 --> 00:01:03,188
<i>they will find out about you.</i>

27
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:04,397
<i>And I mean everybody.</i>

28
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:06,483
[JORDAN]
<i>So, wait. You think it's really him?</i>

29
00:01:06,566 --> 00:01:09,360
<i>Dude, he invested 30 million in us.</i>

30
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:13,615
<i>It makes no sense if he actually</i>
<i>wants the company to fail.</i>

31
00:01:14,574 --> 00:01:15,825
<i>Peter.</i>

32
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:16,951
<i>- Billy.</i>
<i>- Hi.</i>

33
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:18,078
<i>- Jordan.</i>
<i>- Hi.</i>

34
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:19,079
<i>Hi.</i>

35
00:01:19,829 --> 00:01:21,623
<i>What brings you here?</i>

36
00:01:21,706 --> 00:01:22,999
<i>Um…</i>

37
00:01:23,666 --> 00:01:26,085
<i>Someone tried to leak</i>
<i>our confidential data.</i>

38
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:28,004
<i>Should I be worried?</i>

39
00:01:28,087 --> 00:01:29,047
<i>No.</i>

40
00:01:31,549 --> 00:01:34,928
<i>We just wanted to be</i>
<i>transparent with you, Peter.</i>

41
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:37,222
<i>- Uh, that's why we're here.</i>
- [PETER] <i>Right.</i>

42
00:01:37,305 --> 00:01:40,016
<i>To inform you about the attempted leak</i>

43
00:01:40,099 --> 00:01:42,435
<i>before you hear about it</i>
<i>from someone else.</i>

44
00:01:42,519 --> 00:01:43,812
<i>We want you to hear from us first.</i>

45
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:45,271
<i>- Right, right.</i>
- [JORDAN] <i>Right?</i>

46
00:01:45,355 --> 00:01:46,523
<i>Nothing to worry about.</i>

47
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:48,525
<i>Thank you. I… I appreciate that.</i>

48
00:01:48,608 --> 00:01:49,901
- [PHONE RINGING]
<i>- Thanks. Thanks.</i>

49
00:01:49,984 --> 00:01:50,944
<i>I…</i>

50
00:01:51,027 --> 00:01:53,029
<i>Listen. I… I gotta go.</i>

51
00:01:54,155 --> 00:01:55,156
[BILLY] <i>Okay.</i>

52
00:01:58,535 --> 00:01:59,577
<i>What?!</i>

53
00:01:59,661 --> 00:02:02,413
<i>I warn you, Peter. Okay?</i>

54
00:02:02,497 --> 00:02:05,834
<i>If you talk, I will ruin your life.</i>

55
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:07,544
<i>Mark my words!</i>

56
00:02:07,627 --> 00:02:10,338
[LUCY] <i>You're going to see your eldest?</i>

57
00:02:10,421 --> 00:02:13,883
<i>I'll see if she'll give me</i>
<i>a little more time.</i>

58
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:16,386
<i>After all, I don't have</i>
<i>much time left here anyway.</i>

59
00:02:16,469 --> 00:02:17,345
<i>Maybe she'll…</i>

60
00:02:17,428 --> 00:02:19,514
<i>You're going to tell her</i>
<i>about your illness</i>

61
00:02:19,597 --> 00:02:21,307
<i>so she'll feel sorry for you?</i>

62
00:02:25,228 --> 00:02:29,149
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

63
00:02:43,204 --> 00:02:44,539
<i>Mariela?</i>

64
00:02:54,382 --> 00:02:55,675
What are you doing here?

65
00:02:56,509 --> 00:02:57,510
Why?

66
00:02:57,594 --> 00:03:00,263
Are you the only one
who can enter someone else's house?

67
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:01,931
Mariela, please.

68
00:03:02,015 --> 00:03:03,600
Leave us alone.

69
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:06,144
You messed with our lives first.

70
00:03:08,271 --> 00:03:11,316
If it had happened to you,
you'd be angry too.

71
00:03:11,399 --> 00:03:14,193
So, do you regret what you did?

72
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:16,613
How did we mess with your lives?

73
00:03:16,696 --> 00:03:19,032
What's your real problem
with me and my daughter?

74
00:03:19,115 --> 00:03:21,910
You two are the problem!

75
00:03:21,993 --> 00:03:23,578
So we won't stop

76
00:03:23,661 --> 00:03:27,040
until we get what is rightfully ours!

77
00:03:27,123 --> 00:03:28,791
What is rightfully yours?

78
00:03:28,875 --> 00:03:31,210
I don't know what you're
talking about, Mariela.

79
00:03:33,504 --> 00:03:34,505
This.

80
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:37,342
All of this.

81
00:03:38,968 --> 00:03:40,929
This should've been ours.

82
00:03:41,554 --> 00:03:45,225
Because my daughter and I have nothing.

83
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:47,852
Bea got nothing.

84
00:03:48,811 --> 00:03:52,106
I refuse to let you live a good life here

85
00:03:52,190 --> 00:03:54,442
while we're miserable!

86
00:03:54,525 --> 00:03:58,321
If you don't leave, Mariela,
I'm going to call the police.

87
00:03:58,404 --> 00:04:00,240
[PRECIOUS GRUNTS, GROANS]

88
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:01,991
[GRUNTS ANGRILY, HUFFS]

89
00:04:02,992 --> 00:04:04,452
[MARIELA GRUNTS]

90
00:04:04,535 --> 00:04:06,162
You don't deserve this life!

91
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:08,289
You're the ones who should be suffering!

92
00:04:08,373 --> 00:04:12,585
[KETTLE WHISTLING]

93
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:13,795
[EXCLAIMS]

94
00:04:13,878 --> 00:04:15,171
Come here!

95
00:04:16,631 --> 00:04:17,924
[GRUNTS]

96
00:04:18,007 --> 00:04:20,176
- [BOTH SHOUT]
- [KETTLE CLATTERS]

97
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:22,679
[BOTH GRUNTING]

98
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:27,350
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

99
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:29,519
- [MARIELA GRUNTS]
- [PRECIOUS GASPS]

100
00:04:31,604 --> 00:04:33,106
- [THWACKS]
- [MARIELA GRUNTS]

101
00:04:34,816 --> 00:04:37,986
[FIRE CRACKLING]

102
00:04:38,069 --> 00:04:44,033
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

103
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:46,661
[ABIGAIL] <i>Ma! Ma.</i>

104
00:04:46,744 --> 00:04:47,870
[MARIELA COUGHS]

105
00:04:47,954 --> 00:04:48,788
<i>Ma.</i>

106
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:51,541
[ABIGAIL GRUNTS]

107
00:04:51,624 --> 00:04:52,583
<i>- Oh my God!</i>
<i>- Help!</i>

108
00:04:52,667 --> 00:04:55,295
<i>Ma! Ma!</i>

109
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:56,963
<i>- Take her.</i>
<i>- Ma.</i>

110
00:04:57,046 --> 00:04:59,424
<i>- Help her.</i>
<i>- Help! Ma.</i>

111
00:05:00,508 --> 00:05:02,135
Ma! Ma!

112
00:05:02,218 --> 00:05:08,975
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

113
00:05:11,102 --> 00:05:17,859
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

114
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:57,857
[FIRE CRACKLING IN DISTANCE]

115
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:09,744
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

116
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:30,932
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

117
00:06:37,271 --> 00:06:38,981
[LINE RINGING]

118
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:42,652
- [PHONE RINGING]
- [FIRE CRACKLING]

119
00:06:42,735 --> 00:06:43,861
[LINE RINGING]

120
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:45,279
Precious.

121
00:06:45,363 --> 00:06:46,364
[RINGING CONTINUES]

122
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:47,615
Pick up.

123
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:51,285
[RINGING CONTINUES]

124
00:06:51,369 --> 00:06:52,995
Please, pick up!

125
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,790
[BUSY TONE]

126
00:06:57,667 --> 00:06:59,085
[LINE RINGING]

127
00:06:59,168 --> 00:07:01,546
[PHONE RINGING]

128
00:07:01,629 --> 00:07:03,089
[BUSY TONE]

129
00:07:03,172 --> 00:07:06,801
[UNSETTLING MUSIC SWELLS]

130
00:07:10,471 --> 00:07:14,058
[ENGINE REVVING]

131
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:20,022
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

132
00:07:23,359 --> 00:07:25,194
<i>You wrote this, right?</i>

133
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:27,655
<i>Yeah.</i>

134
00:07:27,738 --> 00:07:29,198
<i>- But…</i>
<i>- I knew it.</i>

135
00:07:29,282 --> 00:07:31,117
<i>But what's written there is true.</i>

136
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,493
<i>Yeah.</i>

137
00:07:33,744 --> 00:07:37,331
<i>But you didn't write this</i>
<i>to express Robbie's feelings for me.</i>

138
00:07:39,375 --> 00:07:42,545
<i>You wrote it to express your feelings…</i>

139
00:07:45,590 --> 00:07:47,133
<i>for someone else.</i>

140
00:07:48,885 --> 00:07:52,096
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

141
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,515
<i>But I don't get it.</i>

142
00:07:55,808 --> 00:07:57,351
<i>What's holding you back?</i>

143
00:07:59,061 --> 00:08:00,897
<i>Why can't you just be honest with her?</i>

144
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:06,068
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

145
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:11,115
<i>I mean, I'm telling you this</i>
<i>as your friend.</i>

146
00:08:14,702 --> 00:08:16,913
<i>Do yourself a favor and talk to Billy.</i>

147
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:20,416
<i>And tell her how much you love her.</i>

148
00:08:24,795 --> 00:08:30,218
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

149
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:35,097
<i>I think, boss, for now,</i>

150
00:08:35,181 --> 00:08:38,684
<i>it's better if you just let her know that</i>
<i>you'll always be there for her.</i>

151
00:08:39,602 --> 00:08:41,562
<i>- Okay.</i>
<i>- Yeah?</i>

152
00:08:41,646 --> 00:08:47,985
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

153
00:08:53,991 --> 00:08:55,743
[FLAMES ERUPT]

154
00:09:02,291 --> 00:09:04,752
[FIRE CRACKLING]

155
00:09:08,506 --> 00:09:09,924
[FLAMES ERUPT]

156
00:09:10,007 --> 00:09:14,887
[COUGHING]

157
00:09:14,971 --> 00:09:21,811
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

158
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:24,855
[COUGHING]

159
00:09:24,939 --> 00:09:28,150
[FIRE EXTINGUISHER HISSING]

160
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:31,487
- [FLAME ROARS]
- [PRECIOUS WHIMPERS]

161
00:09:32,363 --> 00:09:33,698
[FIRE EXTINGUISHER CLINKS]

162
00:09:33,781 --> 00:09:40,454
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

163
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:46,711
[FIRE CRACKLING IN DISTANCE]

164
00:09:46,794 --> 00:09:51,257
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

165
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:52,341
Oliver?

166
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:54,552
- Oliver.
- [GRUNTS SOFTLY]

167
00:09:54,635 --> 00:09:56,429
- Wake up, Oliver.
- Billy?

168
00:09:56,512 --> 00:09:58,055
- Get up.
- Huh?

169
00:09:58,139 --> 00:09:59,473
Put these on.

170
00:09:59,557 --> 00:10:00,891
- Billy! Oliver!
- Auntie?

171
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:02,226
The house is on fire! Let's go!

172
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:03,144
- Come on!
- Go! Go!

173
00:10:03,227 --> 00:10:04,270
Be careful. Move!

174
00:10:04,353 --> 00:10:06,022
- Billy.
- [COUGHING]

175
00:10:06,105 --> 00:10:07,815
Auntie? [PANTS]

176
00:10:07,898 --> 00:10:09,233
Billy, hold on.

177
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:11,277
Here, here, Billy.

178
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:12,945
- Wait here.
- Billy, hurry.

179
00:10:13,029 --> 00:10:14,196
Use this to cover you and Oliver.

180
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:15,406
Let's go! Let's go! Hurry!

181
00:10:15,489 --> 00:10:17,116
Wrap this around you.

182
00:10:17,199 --> 00:10:19,035
Careful, Billy. Slowly!

183
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:20,244
[OLIVER COUGHS]

184
00:10:21,245 --> 00:10:23,164
Do you think
there are still people inside?

185
00:10:23,956 --> 00:10:24,832
What's going on here?

186
00:10:24,915 --> 00:10:26,751
Billy's house is on fire!

187
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:28,127
They're still inside!

188
00:10:28,878 --> 00:10:30,004
Careful, Billy!

189
00:10:31,088 --> 00:10:32,673
[WOMAN] Sir, don't go in there!

190
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:34,216
- [MAN] Sir!
- Billy!

191
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:35,968
- [BILLY COUGHS]
- Billy!

192
00:10:37,803 --> 00:10:38,638
[GRUNTS]

193
00:10:38,721 --> 00:10:40,389
Oliver! Billy!

194
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:41,515
Oliver!

195
00:10:41,599 --> 00:10:42,600
[MAN] Get a pail!

196
00:10:42,683 --> 00:10:44,477
[WOMAN] Sir, the fire is spreading!

197
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:46,604
- [PRECIOUS] Oliver! Oliver!
- [BILLY] Auntie!

198
00:10:47,271 --> 00:10:48,689
[PRECIOUS] Oliver! Oliver!

199
00:10:48,773 --> 00:10:50,566
- Get out of here!
- [PRECIOUS] Hurry! Let's go!

200
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:51,817
[OLIVER] Billy!

201
00:10:51,901 --> 00:10:53,611
- [CEILING THUDS]
- [BILLY GASPS]

202
00:10:53,694 --> 00:10:55,154
[BILLY BREATHING HEAVILY]

203
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:58,616
- [ENRICO] Hold on! Move!
- [PRECIOUS COUGHS]

204
00:10:58,699 --> 00:11:00,660
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

205
00:11:00,743 --> 00:11:03,913
- [ENRICO GRUNTING]
- [METAL GATE CLANGING]

206
00:11:03,996 --> 00:11:06,499
- Hurry! Get out!
- Oliver.

207
00:11:06,999 --> 00:11:08,459
- Oliver!
- Auntie.

208
00:11:09,335 --> 00:11:10,711
[BILLY SOBBING] Help!

209
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:12,338
- Oliver!
- Oliver!

210
00:11:12,421 --> 00:11:13,756
[BILLY SCREAMS] Help!

211
00:11:13,839 --> 00:11:15,341
Oliver! Oliver!

212
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:16,759
- Auntie Pres!
- Jordan!

213
00:11:16,842 --> 00:11:18,511
Jordan, Billy's still inside!

214
00:11:19,428 --> 00:11:20,846
[ENRICO COUGHS]

215
00:11:21,597 --> 00:11:22,556
[JORDAN BREATHES HEAVILY]

216
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:24,183
- Billy!
- [BILLY SOBBING]

217
00:11:24,266 --> 00:11:25,101
Stay there!

218
00:11:27,603 --> 00:11:31,065
- [JORDAN GRUNTS]
- [BILLY SOBBING]

219
00:11:32,566 --> 00:11:33,859
Are you hurt?

220
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:37,238
Can you get up?

221
00:11:42,451 --> 00:11:44,620
We're here! Sir, over here!

222
00:11:45,871 --> 00:11:47,206
[JORDAN, BILLY COUGH]

223
00:11:48,916 --> 00:11:50,543
Oliver! Oliver?

224
00:11:50,626 --> 00:11:52,211
They're okay now. It's okay.

225
00:11:52,294 --> 00:11:53,379
Billy.

226
00:11:53,462 --> 00:11:54,588
We'll follow them.

227
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:57,508
- Okay.
- It's okay.

228
00:11:57,591 --> 00:11:58,801
[VOICE TREMBLING] Okay.

229
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:00,719
[AMBULANCE DOOR CLOSES]

230
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:02,096
Okay. [SNIFFLES]

231
00:12:02,179 --> 00:12:04,723
[SIREN WAILING]

232
00:12:04,807 --> 00:12:08,227
[FIRE CRACKLING AGGRESSIVELY]

233
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:09,895
[BILLY SOBBING]

234
00:12:17,736 --> 00:12:23,409
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

235
00:12:26,537 --> 00:12:27,872
[MUSIC FADES]

236
00:12:27,955 --> 00:12:31,417
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

237
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,752
- [DOCTOR] Vital signs?
- Pulse 120, Doc.

238
00:12:33,836 --> 00:12:36,172
BP, 130/80.

239
00:12:36,255 --> 00:12:38,549
O2 sat, 82% on room air.

240
00:12:38,632 --> 00:12:41,886
[DOCTOR] Possible smoke inhalation injury.
Transfer him to Trauma Bay 2 now!

241
00:12:41,969 --> 00:12:44,555
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

242
00:12:44,638 --> 00:12:45,764
[MUSIC FADES]

243
00:12:45,848 --> 00:12:47,683
We've been able to stabilize
his vitals for now.

244
00:12:47,766 --> 00:12:49,185
He's for further evaluation.

245
00:12:49,852 --> 00:12:51,770
But he's still in critical condition.

246
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:55,816
Doc, why isn't he awake yet?

247
00:12:56,442 --> 00:12:58,652
His blood sugar level dropped.

248
00:12:58,736 --> 00:13:00,571
But we've corrected it already.

249
00:13:00,654 --> 00:13:02,281
Let's give it time.

250
00:13:02,364 --> 00:13:04,492
We will keep him under observation.

251
00:13:05,159 --> 00:13:07,578
In the meantime,
I'll let you review the consent

252
00:13:07,661 --> 00:13:10,206
for the limitations of
the procedures he'll undergo.

253
00:13:10,289 --> 00:13:16,837
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

254
00:13:18,589 --> 00:13:20,090
How's your cough? You feel better now?

255
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:29,099
Hmm. How do you feel?

256
00:13:29,183 --> 00:13:30,434
I'm okay.

257
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:31,977
You don't feel dizzy anymore?

258
00:13:32,561 --> 00:13:33,521
Billy,

259
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:35,481
how is Papa?

260
00:13:36,315 --> 00:13:37,316
He's okay.

261
00:13:38,567 --> 00:13:40,319
He still needs to get better.

262
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:46,325
That's why you also need
to get better, okay?

263
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:49,662
You should rest, okay?

264
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:56,752
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

265
00:14:05,594 --> 00:14:07,263
Lord God, thank you so much

266
00:14:07,346 --> 00:14:09,265
for the blessing you've given us.

267
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:13,269
We'll share it among ourselves
while learning Your holy words.

268
00:14:13,352 --> 00:14:14,895
In Jesus' name, amen.

269
00:14:14,979 --> 00:14:16,772
- Amen.
- Amen.

270
00:14:16,855 --> 00:14:22,152
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

271
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:25,823
Man, they already checked
the bars in the kitchen.

272
00:14:25,906 --> 00:14:29,702
But it's bad news.
The metal is still sturdy.

273
00:14:29,785 --> 00:14:34,081
But the railings
by the dumpster are corroded.

274
00:14:34,164 --> 00:14:36,834
That'll be easier to destroy.

275
00:14:36,917 --> 00:14:38,085
Okay?

276
00:14:38,168 --> 00:14:39,420
- Amen.
- Amen.

277
00:14:39,503 --> 00:14:44,300
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

278
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:45,551
[MUSIC FADES]

279
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:51,473
[MACHINE BEEPING]

280
00:14:52,099 --> 00:14:56,270
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

281
00:14:56,353 --> 00:14:59,857
[YOUNG BILLY] <i>Please don't leave us, Dad!</i>
<i>Please don't leave.</i>

282
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:03,110
[SOBBING] <i>Please!</i>

283
00:15:05,529 --> 00:15:06,405
<i>Mommy, please--</i>

284
00:15:06,488 --> 00:15:09,658
<i>Don't waste your tears on worthless men.</i>

285
00:15:09,742 --> 00:15:11,493
<i>We don't need him.</i>

286
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:13,996
<i>We can live without him.</i>

287
00:15:20,669 --> 00:15:22,796
[YOUNG BILLY SNIFFLES, SOBS]

288
00:15:25,049 --> 00:15:26,258
[ENRICO] <i>Please hear me out.</i>

289
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:28,552
<i>I know I did you wrong,</i>

290
00:15:29,094 --> 00:15:30,971
<i>but forgive me, dear!</i>

291
00:15:32,681 --> 00:15:35,309
<i>Dear, let me explain--</i>

292
00:15:35,392 --> 00:15:36,852
<i>That's not necessary.</i>

293
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:39,688
<i>We're fine now.</i>

294
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:44,443
<i>Just leave.</i>

295
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:48,530
<i>Dear, I'm begging you.</i>

296
00:15:48,614 --> 00:15:50,658
<i>No, I am begging you.</i>

297
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:57,581
<i>Let this be the last time</i>
<i>we see each other.</i>

298
00:15:57,665 --> 00:15:59,375
[BILLY SNIFFLES, BREATHES SHAKILY]

299
00:16:04,463 --> 00:16:06,465
- [ENRICO COUGHING]
- [PRECIOUS]<i> Oliver! Oliver!</i>

300
00:16:06,548 --> 00:16:08,384
<i>- Get out of here!</i>
- [PRECIOUS] <i>Hurry! Let's go!</i>

301
00:16:08,467 --> 00:16:09,551
[OLIVER] <i>Billy!</i>

302
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:11,303
- [CEILING THUDS]
- [BILLY GASPS]

303
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:16,100
Billy.

304
00:16:17,267 --> 00:16:19,937
Billy, the cops are here.

305
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:21,855
Okay.

306
00:16:21,939 --> 00:16:27,528
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

307
00:16:27,611 --> 00:16:28,696
[MUSIC FADES]

308
00:16:32,449 --> 00:16:33,617
[DOOR OPENS]

309
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:38,122
Ma?

310
00:16:38,205 --> 00:16:39,039
Ma.

311
00:16:39,123 --> 00:16:40,416
Where have you been?

312
00:16:40,499 --> 00:16:42,418
You weren't answering my calls.

313
00:16:42,501 --> 00:16:44,378
Our problem is over.

314
00:16:44,461 --> 00:16:46,463
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

315
00:16:46,547 --> 00:16:47,965
What do you mean?

316
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:51,593
Now that Billy and her family are gone,

317
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:54,680
we've finally had our revenge
on the family

318
00:16:54,763 --> 00:16:56,682
who took away your father.

319
00:16:57,766 --> 00:17:00,227
And on your father as well.

320
00:17:00,310 --> 00:17:06,025
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

321
00:17:15,868 --> 00:17:17,036
[MUSIC FADES]

322
00:17:21,373 --> 00:17:22,958
- Ma'am.
- Good evening.

323
00:17:23,042 --> 00:17:24,752
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

324
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:26,211
I'll just give you the latest update.

325
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:30,841
We're still looking for Mariela Mercado
and her daughter, Beatrice.

326
00:17:30,924 --> 00:17:34,053
We will let you know
as soon as we have any leads.

327
00:17:34,136 --> 00:17:38,057
We've also obtained CCTV footage.
We already sent it to you.

328
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,224
Okay.

329
00:17:39,308 --> 00:17:42,853
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

330
00:17:42,936 --> 00:17:43,896
Thanks.

331
00:17:43,979 --> 00:17:45,439
All right. Let's go.

332
00:18:00,287 --> 00:18:02,790
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

333
00:18:02,873 --> 00:18:04,583
She kept on yelling.

334
00:18:04,666 --> 00:18:06,585
She was yelling at me.

335
00:18:06,668 --> 00:18:08,045
She said…

336
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:12,800
She said we took what's theirs.

337
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:19,556
<i>If you hadn't stolen LoveFeast,</i>

338
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:22,518
<i>I wouldn't have thought</i>
<i>of something much better.</i>

339
00:18:22,601 --> 00:18:23,811
<i>Okay, then.</i>

340
00:18:24,478 --> 00:18:25,729
<i>I did steal it.</i>

341
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:28,190
<i>But the question is,</i>

342
00:18:29,691 --> 00:18:32,194
<i>which one of us is the bigger thief?</i>

343
00:18:34,279 --> 00:18:35,322
<i>A thief?</i>

344
00:18:37,699 --> 00:18:39,159
<i>What the hell are you talking about?</i>

345
00:18:41,411 --> 00:18:42,996
<i>If only you knew.</i>

346
00:18:45,749 --> 00:18:48,544
Bea told me the exact same thing, Auntie.

347
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:50,712
Do you think…

348
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:56,051
Billy, do you think Bea is aware

349
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:57,970
of what her mom is doing?

350
00:19:00,013 --> 00:19:01,473
They came for LoveList.

351
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:05,227
And now our house too.

352
00:19:05,936 --> 00:19:08,689
Who are they going to ruin next,
Auntie Pres?

353
00:19:08,772 --> 00:19:10,649
You? Oliver?

354
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:12,568
My father?

355
00:19:12,651 --> 00:19:16,947
[MUSIC TURNS SUSPENSEFUL]

356
00:19:33,881 --> 00:19:37,593
<i>CCTV footage revealed</i>
<i>a woman entering the property</i>

357
00:19:37,676 --> 00:19:39,845
<i>shortly before the fire started.</i>

358
00:19:39,928 --> 00:19:42,890
<i>Police have identified her</i>
<i>as Mariela Mercado.</i>

359
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:44,766
[MARIELA]
<i>Why should I be punished?</i>

360
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:47,352
<i>I'll find a way to get you out</i>
<i>of this. I'll protect you.</i>

361
00:19:47,436 --> 00:19:49,938
<i>I'll do whatever it takes</i>
<i>to keep you out of jail, okay?</i>

362
00:19:50,022 --> 00:19:54,902
<i>I'm sorry the condo is a bit small.</i>
<i>But we'll be fine here.</i>

363
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:57,905
[BEA] <i>You're Caloy's friend.</i>
<i>Wilfred, right?</i>

364
00:19:57,988 --> 00:20:00,324
[WILFRED]<i> Looks like you and your mom</i>
<i>got caught up big time.</i>

365
00:20:00,991 --> 00:20:02,910
<i>When are we going back</i>
<i>to the hospital?</i>

366
00:20:02,993 --> 00:20:06,496
<i>Auntie Pres will be</i>
<i>looking after Dad.</i>

367
00:20:07,122 --> 00:20:09,958
<i>Uh, just let me know if you need help</i>

368
00:20:10,042 --> 00:20:12,085
<i>bringing Enrico's stuff to the hospital.</i>

369
00:20:17,507 --> 00:20:20,135
<i>I need 10 million pesos in cash, or else!</i>

370
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:22,095
<i>That's too much, Bea!</i>

371
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:24,681
<i>You will give me 10 million pesos cash,</i>

372
00:20:24,765 --> 00:20:28,310
<i>or bye-bye lawyer, bye-bye wife,</i>
<i>bye-bye family!</i>
